    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508-a4">

                <pb facs="0932" n="872" xml:id="pg872"/>

                <head>Rear-Admiral Turner to Mr. Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 20, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General:</hi> I have received your letter. I
                    deeply sympathize, like yourself, with the sufferers of this world-wide
                    calamity. I do not ask if they are Peruvians of Americans; they are
                    fellow-beings.</p>
                <p>Send whom you wish to my ship, or at least to the flag-ship; Captain McDougal is
                    her captain. We will try and take care of them to Arica. Truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>T. TURNER, <hi rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral, U. S.
                    N.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Major General <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. P.Hovey.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
